o scattered to benefit from exposing [W5,W6,W7]. Taking Chi W5 would leave me with only 7 tiles that don't form good combinations, and I would lose valuable concealment bonuses. With multiple pairs in hand (W5, W7, T7, B6) and good tile availability in unshown tiles, I should maintain flexibility and wait for better opportunities to form a stronger winning hand.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
