his meld loses concealed hand bonuses\n5. The table shows many tiles already discarded; game is progressing\n\nGiven the limited remaining tiles and that I already have one exposed meld [T1, T2, T3], losing concealed hand bonus isn't critical. However, Chi W6 doesn't significantly improve my winning chances since I have better development potential in the B-suit with abundant tiles available.\n\nReason: Passing maintains better flexibility. The B-suit has excellent tile availability (B4, B5, B6, B7, B8 all have 3-4 tiles remaining), which offers stronger winning potential than committing to the W5-W6-W7 meld now. I can still form W5-W6-W7 later if needed (3 W6 remain unshown). Keeping the hand more flexible allows me to pursue multiple winning patterns based on upcoming draws.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
